<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss file appeal in SGS tax case.</title>
<headline>Swiss file appeal in SGS tax case.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss federal tax authorities have lodged an appeal against a tax panel's ruling that upheld Societe Generale de Surveiilance Holding SA (SGS) position in a dispute over share buybacks, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The Swiss Federal Appeals Commission for Tax Matters on May 7 backed SGS's stance that issuing put options to shareholders for buybacks does not represent a taxable distribution subject to the 35 percent withholding tax.</p>
<p>Markets are following the case closely to gauge the potential impact on share buybacks in Switzerland. It was not immediately clear when the Federal Court would rule in the case.</p>
<p>SGS bearer shares were down 60 Swiss francs to 3,150 in early trading.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
